title: Paroxysmal Nocturnal Haemoglobinuria
---

# Paroxysmal Nocturnal Haemoglobinuria

- **Definition** - a rare benign non-malignant clonal expansion of haematopoietic stem cell deficient in GPI-anchor protein
- **Pathophysiology** - increased Sn of RBC to lysis by complements
- **Clinical associations:**
  - Hypoplastic bone marrow failure
  - Aplastic anaemia
  - Myelodysplastic syndrome
- **Clinical features:**
  - Early morning coca-cola urine reflecting intravascular haemolysis
  - Hyper-coagulable states (e.g. Portal vein thrombosis, splenic vein thrombosis)
- **Mx** - supportive w/ blood transfusions and Tx of thrombosis
